\name{cellucid_cells_values}
\alias{cellucid_cells_values}
\title{Read values of cells}
\usage{
cellucid_cells_values(viewer, cells, fields)
}
\arguments{
\item{viewer}{A viewer \code{\link{cellucid_view}()} or \code{\link{cellucid_serve}()} returned.}
\item{cells}{Cells: 1-based positions, \code{TRUE}/\code{FALSE} for every cell, or the cell names of the object the viewer shows, each once (sent as original positions). Required.}
\item{fields}{A vector or list of a named list (at least 1 item). Required.}
}
\value{
A \code{cellucid_action_request}, at once and invisibly: the action is sent now, or when the viewer's channel opens.
\code{\link{cellucid_action_result}(request)} returns what it read: a list of \code{cells} (The cells asked for that are open, in the order asked), \code{columns}, \code{not_open} (Cells asked for that are not open (a subsample)). Cells in it are original positions (0-based rows of the dataset's obs).
}
\description{
The values of named cells (original positions) in each field or gene asked for.
}
\details{
The viewer's action \code{cells.values} (Dataset). It reads, and changes nothing: it makes no step of the history.
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{cellucid_act}()} sends any action by its type, and \code{\link{cellucid_action_result}()}
